apple released the airpods max over a  year ago in december of 2020 and when my  brother first bought his pair he let me  listen to them and i can tell you that i  was totally blown away by the sound  quality and now that we're in 2020 i  have finally caved and i bought my own  personal pair of airpods max so in this  video what i'm gonna do is explain why i  finally caved after so long and i'm  gonna share my experience and my review  over the past couple of weeks that have  owned these and then i'm going to  explain why i think i may have made a  mistake and why i might actually return  them but before we get into all of that  let's first start off with my story and  why i finally decided to buy these  airpods max now the first time i heard  them i really really wanted to buy them  but the problem was that we just spent a  bunch of money on remodeling my house so  i couldn't afford it back then and i've  been really craving it ever since then  but i could never justify the price  because i mean  550 dollars is a ton of money to give  for a pair of headphones and if you want  a completely honest reason for why i  finally bought these well there are  actually two of them first of all these  are finally on sale on amazon for a  really good price  479 dollars so it's definitely a good  discount and the second reason is that i  actually got a christmas bonus so i  could finally justify it because it's  kind of like a bonus with work and all  that so i finally bought these because  of the bonus but don't worry that's  actually not the only reason because the  recent reviews for the airpods max have  actually been getting a lot more  positive with people saying that the  reliability has been getting better the  software and even the sound quality  improvements themselves and new features  like the spatial audio with all of that  making for a much better product  compared to when these initially  launched so with that said let me  finally get into my experience in my  review of these after owning them for  the first couple of weeks well first of  all the sound quality is very very  impressive the base is good the highs  are good and it actually is better than  when i first heard them over a year ago  now on top of that the new spatial audio  feature works incredibly well and it  just blows my mind how it sounds like  you're in the room or you're in the  auditorium or in the studio with all the  sounds coming from different locations  around you and it's just so immersive  and to be honest it kind of gives for  like this emotional or kind of connected  listening experience which is what you  really want with headphones it kind of  like puts you in a different world it's  really weird but on top of that it also  works very very well with the apple  ecosystem like for example how i  connected them to my iphone and then  they were automatically connected on my  mac and it worked just so well with no  issues with switching from my iphone to  my mac it's just been so very reliable  and i'm very impressed with how good  these have been so everything from the  auto pause feature when you take them  off your head and put them back on it  works very well including all the  buttons the side button the digital  crown with changing the volume all of  that just works very reliably and i'm  very impressed by that but what really  surprised me was the battery life the  battery life on these things is  absolutely insane after i first unboxed  them i didn't plug them in for the first  couple of days and i was honestly  surprised that like wow these things are  lasting that long and in the past couple  of weeks i've literally only plugged  them in three times and that's not even  when they hit zero percent it was like  25 and then i would plug them in like  these things last forever but on top of  that the build quality is very very  solid so i don't even worry about  dropping these because there's no way  these would break you just got metal  everywhere compared to other plastic  headphones like in the past when i would  drop them and then it would crack and  unfortunately you got to buy a new pair  i literally do not think these will  crack if you drop them and then one  thing that absolutely blew my mind was  the performance of the noise  cancellation it just works  mind-blowingly well like you could play  some music have it on and you literally  can't hear anything around you but then  on the other hand the noise cancellation  is also very good for when you just want  to calm down and listen to some quiet  music with the noise cancellation  because you don't hear any background  noise and you just have some calm music  that's not at full blast so it just gets  rid of all of the background noise and  now because the noise cancellation is so  good almost like it's too good this  could actually cause a problem while i'm  at home because i do have a young son  he's almost two years old and if he  wakes up from a nap or maybe he falls or  something like that i won't be able to  hear him and thankfully there is the  transparency mode which is really really  awesome because the way it works is it  records your surroundings with the  microphones and then it plays them into  your ears while sounding incredibly  natural almost like you don't even have  anything on your head so with that said  i could just turn the volume up to  around 50 percent and still hear what's  going on in my house without worrying  about something happening so to sum up  my experience over the last couple weeks  i've got to say that i'm very very  impressed with the airpods max and i  don't regret spending that much money on  sale 480  on these headphones but unfortunately  with all of that said i think there's a  chance that i may have made a mistake by  buying them right now and i'm actually  considering returning them because of  something that happened last week let me  explain if you didn't already know mark  german is the most reliable apple leaker  out there and he was recently the guest  on mac rumor's new podcast where he  mentioned all the new products we should  be expecting from apple and one thing  that he mentioned was that we could  actually be seeing a new version of  airpods max with new colors later this  year yes this year now this shocked me  because i wasn't expecting a new version  until maybe next year 2023 but he thinks  it's coming this year and then on top of  that mark thinks that there's actually a  chance that the new version of the  airpods max could switch to a usbc port  instead of lightning which would  actually be a huge deal for a lot of the  people out there who are sick of having  the lightning port especially since the  chance that the upcoming iphone 14 pro  might come with a usbc port and if that  happens apple is probably going to get  rid of lightning across all their  products probably within a year or two  and finally mark says that we could  probably expect to see better battery  life on the new model as well and that  last point got me thinking because of a  recent video i made about the airpods  pro 2 coming with lossless audio support  and the way i think apple is going to do  this is by adopting their new ultra  wideband technology with the u1 chip  that they've been putting into every  iphone since the iphone 11 as well as  both the apple watch series 6 the 7 and  probably the upcoming eight and the  beauty of ultra wideband technology is  that it can potentially use 10 times  less battery life compared to bluetooth  as well as drastically reducing latency  close to as low as wired accessories and  of course it also offers massive amounts  of bandwidth up to  675 megabits per second compared to only  around two with bluetooth so with that  said i fully believe that the airpods  pro 2 are gonna have lossless support  just like mitraq claimed a couple of  weeks ago and i think that if apple  releases new airpods max later this year  then they're also gonna support ultra  wide band or whatever else apple adopts  to bring lossless and yes that means  that you're going to be able to play  high-resolution lossless apple music  with the next airpods max without any  wires and because of all of that i'm  starting to wonder if i made a mistake  by buying these airpods max over a year  after they came out and i'm wondering if  i should just return these right now and  wait for the new ones to come well in  reality there's a chance that they're  actually not going to come this year and  then that would be very unfortunate if i  returned these ones and now that i think  about it these have honestly been so  nice over the past couple of weeks that  i'm actually willing to lose some resale  value at the end of this year if new  ones do come out and i decided to  replace these with the new ones so with  all that said i've got to say that for  the full package that you're getting  especially having them work so reliably  with the apple ecosystem and of course  the awesome battery life i definitely  say that they're worth it for that sale  price of 479 on amazon and the really  solid build quality means that you could  keep them for the next 5 or maybe even  10 years if you don't really care about  new features like lossless supports and  that definitely makes these worth it so  there you guys go hopefully you enjoyed  the video and if you did go ahead and  click the circle above to subscribe and  definitely check out my airpods pro 2  lossless support video right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

